  "detail": "Thank you for the differential test and the benchmark; they show exactly where the time goes. Measured in this PR: 20,000 strings took 157 s (7.9 ms each) against 166 s before, so a verify session still spends minutes of main-thread time and stalls the daemon. Measured on this PR's benchmark holdout (132 static details): a fresh combined pattern costs 5.4 ms per call including its first-use compile (JavaScriptCore compiles lazily), against 0.074 ms for a reused one; each observed literal's boundary test against the 20 KB public sources costs about 0.05 ms. The cause, as the report says, is that any value with observed literals not already in the detail set compiles a new alternation regex over all static and observed details (hundreds of Unicode lookbehind alternatives) on every call. Required: never compile a regex over the static details per call. Precompile one static pattern per invocation (sorted by length, as today). Per call, collect the value's observed private literals (with the cached publicSources boundary test), drop those already in the static set, and compile a small pattern over only the remaining observed literals, sorted by length. Then replace in one left-to-right pass that reproduces the combined alternation exactly. Using `g` regexes and `lastIndex`, find the next static match and the next observed match from the current position. Take the one that starts first; if both start at the same index, take the longer; on equal length take the static one, which comes first in today's stable sort because static details are inserted before observed ones. Replace it, continue from its end, and re-search either pattern whose pending match started before that end. Keep the `[private detail]` placeholder, the removed count and the `[n private details withheld]` suffix exactly as today. Keep the differential test (all outputs identical to the frozen implementation) and extend its generator with overlapping static/observed details, equal-length ties and adjacent matches. Rerun the benchmark: the total must fall by at least 10x and the worst call should be a few milliseconds; report both in the PR. Run only test/verification.test.ts and the other directly affected tests, `bunx biome check` on the changed files and `bunx tsc --noEmit`."
 }
